# Trivy ignore list — reviewed 2026-08-07
#
# Each entry needs a reason and a re-check trigger. Do not add a CVE here
# just to make CI green; if it is fixable in our dependencies, fix it.

# CVE-2026-69192 — ip-address <10.3.1, SSRF via inconsistent IP parsing.
#
# Not reachable through our dependency tree. This copy lives inside npm's
# own bundled deps at /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/ip-address,
# not in /app/node_modules, so no change to package.json can move it.
# npm 12.0.2 is the current latest and still bundles 10.2.0, so there is no
# npm release to upgrade to. Removing npm is not an option either: the
# entrypoint runs `npx prisma migrate deploy` at container start.
#
# Exposure in this image is nil — the vulnerable code path is npm's
# registry/proxy URL handling, and the container never runs npm against a
# network registry; it only invokes the local prisma CLI against SQLite.
#
# Re-check when npm >12.0.2 ships: if it bundles ip-address >=10.3.1, bump
# the pin in Dockerfile and delete this entry.
CVE-2026-69192

# CVE-2026-14257, CVE-2026-69152 — brace-expansion <5.0.9, DoS via memory
# exhaustion / unbounded intermediate arrays in expand().
#
# Same situation as the entry above: this copy is npm's own bundled dep at
# /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/brace-expansion (5.0.7), not
# in /app/node_modules. brace-expansion 5.0.9 exists, but no npm release
# bundles it yet, so the Dockerfile pin cannot reach it.
#
# Exposure is nil: expand() is called on glob patterns npm itself parses,
# and the container runs one fixed command (`prisma migrate deploy`) with no
# attacker-controlled glob input. Both CVEs are DoS-only, no code execution.
#
# Re-check when npm >12.0.2 ships. Worth noting the Dockerfile's global npm
# upgrade was originally added (06b1bb8) to patch exactly this package —
# npm's bundled deps go stale faster than npm releases, so the better
# long-term fix is to drop the global npm from the runner entirely and have
# docker-entrypoint.sh call ./node_modules/.bin/prisma instead of `npx`.
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152
